WEBVTT

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.980
Wendy, they're dead!

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:10.990
Brody, pull it together.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.580
We don't have a chance, okay?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.980
We have to get out of here now!

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.560
No, Brody.We are not leaving.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.210
We have got to find my sister.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:17.950
No!

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.800
No, I am getting out of here right now!

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.740
Brody!

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.220
Brody, get back here!

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.640
Brody!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.070
God, you son of a bitch!

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.620
Cut.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.540
What the hell was that?

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:55.470
Thanks.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:58.460
Here you go.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.730
Thanks, Walter.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.230
Don't mark that.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.290
It's all good, Tara.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.750
That was great.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.940
Uh, let's do it again.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.630
Uh, maybe we try dialing
up that scream, huh?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:12.540
I know, I know.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.810
I'm just -- I'm having
trouble with the tennis ball.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.060
That is just for cg registration.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.870
When ivan and the fx guys are done,
it is going to look terrifying.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.630
You want to look at the
concept sketches again?

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:24.660
No, that's okay.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.530
I'll find it.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.100
I know you will, pumpkin, huh?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:27.990
Okay.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.350
Going again, everybody.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.980
10-Minute reload for camera and sound.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.130
No, man, I'm telling you.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:40.530
Working alone behind the sets or after
wrap, I catch this weird vibe sometimes.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.020
Like what?

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.990
Mmm, like something's watching.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.980
Come on.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.230
Hey.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.930
Working on a movie like this?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.070
Weird crap's bound to happen.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.680
Frank thinks the stage is
haunted. Like, for real.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:00.840
All I'm saying is, they call wrap,
I get done, and I get out of here.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.360
Fast.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.370
Guy is definitely off his meds.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.560
Brody, come back.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.020
You son of a bitch.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.660
Brody, come back, you son of a bitch.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.900
Hello?

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.190
Guys?

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.580
Come on.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.580
It's not funny.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.670
Okay.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.810
Ha ha, very funny.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.570
Hello?

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.280
Who's there?

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.740
Now, that's what I'm talking about!

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:50.260
First opened in 1927, the lot has been
in continuous operation for eight decades.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.810
Hey, you know this is where
they filmed "Creepshow"?

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.540
Now to the right here is Stars Hollow.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.390
It's the setting for the
television series "Gilmore Girls."

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:08.020
And if we're lucky, we might even
catch one of the show's stars.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.470
Come on.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.150
Let's finish the tour.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:18.040
And then up to the right here, we have New York
Avenue, and that's where they shot "Lois & Clark."

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.480
Sammy, check it out.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.090
It's matt damon.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.430
Yeah.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.730
I'm pretty sure that's not Matt Damon.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.590
No, it is.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.550
Well, Matt Damon just picked
up a broom and started sweeping.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.700
Yeah, he was probably
researching a role or something.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.840
Uh, I don't think so.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.110
Hey, this way.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.180
Uh, I think stage 9's over here.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:39.780
Come on, man.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:40.770
Let's keep going this way.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:41.500
No, come on.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.260
We got to work.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:42.950
Golly.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.140
Dude, you wanted to come to L.A.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.340
Yeah, for a vacation!

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.710
I mean, swimming pools and movie stars!

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:48.770
Not to work.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.290
This seem like swimming
pool weather to you, Dean?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.760
It's practically canadian.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.030
Yeah.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:59.720
I just figured that, you know, after everything that happened
with madison, you could use a little R&R,  that's all.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.790
Maybe I want to work, Dean.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.090
Maybe it keeps my mind off things.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.000
Okay, okay, all right.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.830
So this crew guy, what,
did he ...he died on set?

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.160
Yeah, rumors spreading
like wildfire online.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.270
They're saying the set's haunted.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.820
Like "poltergeist"?

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.160
Could be a poltergeist.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:15.730
No, no, no.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.420
The movie "poltergeist."

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.910
You know nothing of your
cultural heritage, do you?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:27.010
It was rumored that the set of "poltergeist" was
cursed, that they used real human bones as props.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.600
Like, at least three of
the actors died in it.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:32.810
Yeah, might be something like that.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.740
All right, so this crew guy.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.680
What's his name?

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.930
Frank Jaffe.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.080
You got a death certificate
or a coroner's report?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.920
Well, no, but, uh, it's L.A., You know?

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.340
That might not even be his real name.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.120
But the girl who found him, she said
she saw something ... a vanishing figure.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.120
What's the girl's name?

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.080
Uh, Tara Benchley.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.260
Whoa, Tara Benchley?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.260
From "feardotcom" and
"ghost ship" Tara Benchley?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.100
Dude, why didn't you say so?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.440
So now you're suddenly on board?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.110
I mean, I'm a fan of her work.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.490
It's very good.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:06.790
No, look.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.510
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.420
Everyone at this studio loves
the dailies, myself included.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.990
We were just wondering if it could be...

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.850
You know, a little brighter.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:16.470
Brighter?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.650
Yeah, Jay, more color.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:19.790
Mcg, you know what I'm saying.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.140
You're the master of that stuff.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.880
Brad, this is a horror movie.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.550
Who says horror has to be dark?

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:27.720
It's just -- It's sort of
depressing, don't you think?

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:28.650
Uh, excuse me.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.530
Uh, green-Shirt guy?

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.110
Yeah, yeah, you.Come here.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:37.140
Can you get me a, uh,
smoothie from craft?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.060
You want a what from who?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.250
You are a P.A.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.560
This is what you do.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.540
Yeah, he, uh...

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.030
One smoothie coming right up.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.530
What's a P.A.?

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.580
I think they're kind of like slaves.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.100
They'll let anybody
in this business, huh?

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.190
6, 6, 6. Mark.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.620
Ready!

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.500
Okay, why don't we take it
from, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.720
And action.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:46.280
Come on.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.660
It'll be fun.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.590
Dicta sunt explicabo.

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.000
God, I hate you so much right now.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.180
Cut!

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.360
Very nice.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.930
So?

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.710
No emf anywhere.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.400
Great.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.190
So, what do you think?

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:36.200
Well, I think being a P.A.Sucks, but...

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.220
But the food these people get?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:38.840
Are you kidding me?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.260
I mean, look at these things.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.490
They're like miniature
philly cheesesteak sandwiches.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:44.940
They're delicious.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.420
Maybe later.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.060
What did you find out
about the dead crew guy?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.030
Uh, Frank Jaffe was just
filling in for the day.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.370
Nobody here knew him or
where he lived or anything.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:00.950
Oh, great.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.200
So you found out about as much as I did.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.120
Hey, guys.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.170
Oh, hey.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.630
They're wonderful.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:07.680
Listen.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.850
I did dig up some stuff
about stage 9's history.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:15.260
Four people died messy here over the past 80
years, two suicides and two fatal accidents.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.890
Any one of those could
be a vengeful spirit.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.220
Yeah.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.100
Just got to narrow it down more.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.150
I'll get right on that.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.260
Hey, are you supposed
to get one of these?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.920
I..I don't really know what I'm doing.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.060
First day?

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.980
Yeah, my big break.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:58.550
You know, I know it's really uncool
to say this, but I'm a big fan.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.750
I loved you in "boogeyman."

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.730
Oh, god.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.760
What a terrible script.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.100
Uh, but, thank you.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.610
Yeah.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:09.590
You found him, right?

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.850
The -- The
dead guy?

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:16.330
I'm sorry.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.720
You probably don't
want to talk about this.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.190
No, no, actually,
it's -- It's okay.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.660
Nobody around here really
brings it up very much.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.120
I think they're all scared I'm
gonna have some kind of breakdown.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:29.020
That must have been awful.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.310
What happened?

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.100
It was horrible.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:42.730
There ... there was all this blood coming
from his eyes, from his mouth, and, uh...

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.990
I saw this, um...

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:49.830
What?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.010
I saw this shape.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.970
To tell you the truth, I
don't know actually what I saw.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:00.770
I just know I saw it.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.830
Thanks, Walter.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:09.940
Uh, so this -- This crew
guy Frank, did you know him?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.140
No, not that well.

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:12.730
That's funny.

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:15.200
It's like no one around
here actually knew the guy.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.480
I got his picture.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:18.360
You do?

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.150
Yeah.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.510
I take polaroids of all the crew.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.200
It's just one of those things
you do to kill time on the set.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.490
Right there.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.830
Son of a bitch.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:45.210
Gerard st.James?

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.480
Yes?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.310
You're still alive, and
you're not Frank Jaffe.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.510
NO

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:55.180
You were -- You were desert soldier number 4
in "Metalstorm: The destruction of jared-Syn."

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:56.060
I was.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.770
I knew I recognized you.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.670
I am a huge fan.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:04.620
I mean, your turn as the tractor-Crash
victim in "Critters 3" ...wow.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.570
Hey, well, please.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:07.340
Come in.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.270
Thanks.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.470
Yeah, it was the producers.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:20.610
I mean, they brought me in
for the day to play Frank.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.760
Just to fake your death?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.270
Well, rumors of a haunted film set...

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:31.880
Free publicity, especially when you're making a horror
movie I mean, it's already all over the internet.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:33.500
Yeah, we know.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:38.050
These days, it's all about
new media, building buzz.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.250
They say I'm the new "lonelygirl."

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:42.840
Who?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.760
And the ghost Tara saw?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.280
Projected on a screen of diffusion.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.990
Isn't that kind of cruel...

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.380
Messing with their heads like that?

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.390
Hey, I just play the part.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.040
I don't write the script.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.010
Speaking of...

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:03.470
I'm playing willy in a dinner-Theater production
of "salesman" at costa mesa all next month.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:06.430
Get a free pepper steak with the coupon.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.180
Well, now, wait a second.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.510
If you're seen in public,
won't that ruin the hoax?

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:11.750
Oh, please.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.410
Frank and willy, , ,
totally different characters.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.760
You know what?

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:18.760
Thanks very much, Mr. Saint.James.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:19.750
It was just nagging at us.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:24.820
But we're ...we're very glad,
you know, you're alive and well.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:26.160
Yeah.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.290
Absolutely.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.320
I wanted to ask you.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:33.810
What was it like working
with Richard Moll?

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.850
He's from "metalstorm."

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:42.110
He was Hurok, King
of the Cyclops people.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.010
Gentleman's gentleman.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.380
Yeah?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.620
All right.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.100
Pepper steak.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:57.340
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back...back from hell.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.490
Now they're trying to use us...

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:01.880
It doesn't matter.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.030
We're not going till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.380
Got it?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:06.300
Good.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.910
Now, let's get busy.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.690
Cut!

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:11.550
No good for sound.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.490
I'm getting some kind of feedback.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.160
Another costly sound delay.

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.060
All right, we're going
again for sound, people!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.520
Thank you!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.930
No, it's a great scene,
really ..Dynamite.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.080
But I still got a few...

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:29.330
Not -- Not problems,
just questions.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.670
Like what?

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:35.280
Well, for one thing. The rules
aren't really landing for me.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:40.570
Like, the kids do this latin chant,
and that makes the ghosts show up?

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:41.660
Yeah.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.670
If the ghosts are in hell,
how do they hear the chanting?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.580
I mean, what, do they
have super hearing?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:48.680
Well, it's a logic bump.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.310
The rules don't track.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.080
Marty, you're the writer.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.690
What about throwing in an explainer?

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:55.450
Yeah, that'd be super.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.070
I got to check some messages.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.690
Suits.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.260
Has mcg seen this?

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:25.340
I like the whole body-Paint,
black-And-White thing, but, gee, I...

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.460
I don't think those neck wounds
are really gonna read on-Camera.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.770
They need to be red.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.470
You know what I'm saying?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.650
Hey, Jay!

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.640
I need to speak to makeup.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.340
Yeah?

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:01.460
Wait up.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:06.050
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back ...back from hell.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:07.260
I don't understand.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.450
If they were in hell, how
could they hear our chanting?

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:11.380
They must have super hearing.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:46.140
Wendy?

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:46.980
Oh, Mitch!

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.230
God, you're alive!

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:50.000
You won't get rid of me that easy.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.250
Rumble, rumble, rumble!

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:54.270
Salt.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.250
Okay, we need salt.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:58.440
I read in that book that
it keeps ghosts away.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.390
Kendra, logan, you guys check the back.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:04.680
The poor bastard killed
himself, like, for real.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.390
Shouldn't we shut it down or something?

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:09.030
We had a moment of silence
for him at breakfast.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:10.820
He was just a studio guy.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.230
Shh.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.350
I love you.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:14.260
I know.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.170
I'm sorry.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:21.840
Can we ...can we cut or something?

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.200
Uh, yeah.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:24.600
Cut.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.380
Cut!

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.570
That's a cut!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.400
Only I get to say "cut."

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:34.340
Hey, what's up?

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.200
I'm just a little upset.

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:39.850
With everything that's been
going on, who can blame you?

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.750
I just can't wrap my head
around the dialogue, you know?

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.970
"Salt" -- Doesn't
that sound silly?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.480
I mean, why would a
ghost be afraid of salt?

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.100
Okay, um...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.710
Marty, what do you think?

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:53.220
Not married to salt.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:53.770
What do you want?

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.580
We still sticking with condiments?

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.540
Mmm, it just sounds
different, not better.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.120
What else would a ghost be scared of?

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.880
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.400
What would a ghost be scared of?

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:06.160
Maybe shotguns.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:09.620
That makes even less sense than salt.

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.370
These people are idiots.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.280
Walter's a little testy for a P.A., Huh?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.510
How's it going in here?

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:24.930
Really good -- Tara has stepped up her performance,
and I think it's from the sense-Memory stuff.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.770
Sense-Memory?

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:26.890
Yeah.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:31.730
Dean, you know, when I ask how it's going
here, I'm talking about the case, right?

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.330
We don't really work here.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.240
You know, I thought
you hated being a P.A.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:38.990
I don't know.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:39.730
It's not so bad.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:41.590
I kind of feel like part
of the team, you know?

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.420
It's good.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.530
Oh, taquito?

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.700
They're wonderful.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.530
No.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.460
Um, listen.

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:49.030
I conned my way into the morgue.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:50.990
News reports are right.

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:52.640
Brad's a doornail
-- No question.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:53.670
Copy that.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:54.410
Sorry.What?

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:55.270
"Copy that"?

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.040
What did you say?

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.170
The news reports are right.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.010
Brad's a doornail.

00:19:58.010 --> 00:19:58.920
They're aware.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:19:59.840
Who's aware?

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:00.520
Sorry.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:01.460
What were you saying?

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:04.440
Uh, uh, the newspaper's right.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:05.390
Brad's a doornail.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.330
No question about it.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.090
I guess it's a good
thing we didn't skip town.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:09.070
Oh, come here.

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:10.510
I want you to hear something.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.430
Copy that.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.710
On my way.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.480
Hey, Dave.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.540
Can you play that thing
you were playing me earlier?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.910
Sure.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:20.720
Thanks.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:25.540
It doesn't matter.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.840
We're not leaving till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:29.090
Got it?

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:30.240
Good.

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:31.930
Now, let's get busy.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:36.170
E.V.P.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.880
From the night of Brad's stage dive.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.030
All of a sudden, I'm getting
electromagnetic readings up the wazoo.

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:43.210
For some reason, it's
a legit haunting now.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:43.980
Well, whose ghost, Dean?

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:44.710
What's it want?

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.300
I think we should take a
look at Brad's death scene.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:10.550
Now, where'd you get this dvd?

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.090
They're called dailies.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:13.270
I got it from cindy.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:15.480
She's kind of got this
thing going with drew.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.220
He dubbed me an extra copy.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:20.950
All right.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.650
Here's where the guy
fell through the roof.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.170
Right.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.140
All right, here we go.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.940
They must have super hearing.

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:33.400
Wait.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:34.710
Go back, go back.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:37.870
Right after -- Right
after -- Yeah, right.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:39.940
Wait.

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.300
There.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:48.160
It's like "3 men and
a baby" all over again.

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:54.260
Selleck, danson, and guttenberg,
and I don't know who played the baby.

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:55.390
What's your point?

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:58.980
There's a scene where people say that
the camera caught a ghost on film.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:02.210
Apparently, in the background of one of the
scenes, there was this boy that nobody remembers.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:04.130
Spirit photography.

00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:09.830
I've seen her before.

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:16.960
Here.Check this out.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:20.370
Yeah, go for ozzie.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:24.170
No, I don't have a 20 on Tara.

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:25.160
I think she's 10-100.

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:28.800
Okay, copy that.

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:30.130
I'm sorry.

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:31.520
What were you saying?

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:37.370
Elise Drummond. Starlet
back in the '30s.

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:42.870
Had an affair with a studio exec.

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:45.410
He uses her up, fires
her, leaves her destitute.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:49.410
Elise hangs herself from stage 9's rafters
right into a scene they're shooting.

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:50.900
Just like our man Brad.

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:52.840
So, what, she's got it
in for the studio brass?

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:53.970
Possibly.

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:57.420
I mean, it's a motive, and
Brad's death matches hers exactly.

00:22:57.420 --> 00:22:59.490
We're digging tonight, aren't we?

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:02.090
That's a wrap, people!

00:23:02.090 --> 00:23:05.170
6:00 A.M.Call for crew tomorrow.

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:08.390
Great work, everybody!

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:11.640
Mcg, you're a genius.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:14.080
You're kickin' ass and taking names.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:15.330
Good night, Jay.

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:17.400
Yeah.

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:21.410
Which way?

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:23.990
Over here.

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:30.730
Hey.

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:31.880
Yeah?

00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:36.610
Hey, this map is totally
worth the 5 bucks.

00:23:37.050 --> 00:23:40.010
Hey, we got to go check out Johnny
Ramone's grave when we're done here.

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:41.720
You want to dig him up, too?

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:44.080
Bite your tongue, heathen!

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
You know, Dean, what I
don't get is, why now?

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:50.800
I mean, after 75 years, Elise
Drummond suddenly goes homicidal.

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:51.910
You know, why this movie?

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.110
Well, maybe she's mad they're
making a scary ghost flick.

00:23:54.110 --> 00:23:55.500
Is it really that scary?

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:56.550
Here we go.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:01.700
Yahtzee.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:13.140
I know.

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:16.330
No, I friggin' hate mcg's dailies.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:17.690
I can't control the guy.

00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:20.970
I'm telling you -- Next
one I'm directing myself.

00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:22.910
What, you?

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:24.010
No, bob.

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:25.200
You I love.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:26.180
You're a genius.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:28.490
You're kicking ass and taking names.

00:24:28.490 --> 00:24:30.060
Yeah, okay.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:31.080
Yeah.

00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:32.130
Talk to you later, babe.

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:33.410
Uh-Huh.

00:24:33.910 --> 00:24:35.280
What a dick.

00:24:36.650 --> 00:24:38.240
Oh, great.

00:24:41.080 --> 00:24:42.660
Hey, guys!

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:44.620
Producer walking here!

00:24:44.620 --> 00:24:46.350
Hello!

00:25:43.870 --> 00:25:44.870
Hey!

00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:48.080
Hey, pal.

00:25:48.120 --> 00:25:50.190
Can you, uh, show me to the exit?

00:25:50.190 --> 00:25:52.400
I can't see a damn thing here.

00:25:56.630 --> 00:25:57.890
Hey!

00:25:58.310 --> 00:25:59.170
Hey, putz.

00:25:59.170 --> 00:26:00.550
I'm talking to you.

00:26:00.610 --> 00:26:02.330
Somebody could get hurt here.

00:26:09.890 --> 00:26:11.310
What the hell?

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:22.960
No!

00:26:27.300 --> 00:26:28.850
No!

00:26:57.230 --> 00:26:59.130
They never forgive.

00:27:00.330 --> 00:27:02.410
They never forget.

00:27:02.430 --> 00:27:03.650
Mitch?

00:27:04.160 --> 00:27:04.940
Ashley?

00:27:04.940 --> 00:27:08.850
This summer, they're coming
back again to settle the score...

00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:10.350
Again.

00:27:10.850 --> 00:27:12.290
You out here?

00:27:15.480 --> 00:27:16.910
Ashley and Todd
-- They're dead!

00:27:16.910 --> 00:27:18.060
Wendy, they're dead!

00:27:18.060 --> 00:27:20.640
These bastards aren't taking
us, not without a fight.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:22.150
I am getting out of here right now!

00:27:22.150 --> 00:27:23.340
Brody!

00:27:23.770 --> 00:27:26.080
From the makers of
"Cornfield Massacre"...

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:29.300
"Monster truck, " "Charlie's angels"...

00:27:29.300 --> 00:27:30.760
"Charlie's Angels 2: Full throttle"...

00:27:30.760 --> 00:27:35.190
And "Hell hazers" comes a
new experience in terror.

00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:40.050
<i>We must have brought them
back ...back from hell. AGAIN</i>

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:45.090
<i>This film not yet rated</i>

00:27:46.930 --> 00:27:48.970
Rolled in with a giant fan.

00:27:48.970 --> 00:27:52.990
Same thing happened to an electrician
back in '66 -- A guy named Billy Beard.

00:27:52.990 --> 00:27:54.320
What the hell, dude?

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:54.960
I don't know.

00:27:54.960 --> 00:27:57.430
It doesn't seem like Elise this time.

00:27:57.430 --> 00:27:58.240
We already torched her.

00:27:58.240 --> 00:27:59.390
Are we dealing with another ghost?

00:27:59.390 --> 00:28:00.060
Maybe.

00:28:00.060 --> 00:28:02.050
Yeah, but these things
don't usually tag-Team.

00:28:06.260 --> 00:28:07.210
Everybody!

00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:08.800
Gather around, okay?

00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:10.390
I got an announcement to make.

00:28:10.540 --> 00:28:11.910
Hold that for me.

00:28:13.990 --> 00:28:15.020
Everyone!

00:28:15.490 --> 00:28:16.430
Huddle in!

00:28:19.570 --> 00:28:28.880
In light of Jay's accident last night and in cooperation with
the authorities, we're shutting down production for a few days.

00:28:29.400 --> 00:28:31.000
I know, I know.

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.820
Look, I'm not going to lie to you.

00:28:32.820 --> 00:28:35.430
We've had a few setbacks this week.

00:28:35.430 --> 00:28:39.750
But we all know what Jay and
Brad wanted more than anything.

00:28:40.810 --> 00:28:46.380
And that was to see "Hell Hazers 2: The
Reckoning" on screens all across America.

00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:53.230
Now, we owe it to them to go on and to
pull together and make this damn movie, huh?

00:28:54.600 --> 00:28:57.600
But... but ... but ... but
...but not ... not today.

00:28:57.600 --> 00:28:59.330
Go home.

00:28:59.330 --> 00:29:01.090
Someone will call you.

00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:06.360
Wendy.

00:29:06.360 --> 00:29:08.740
What, are you afraid of ghosts?

00:29:08.740 --> 00:29:09.470
Come on.

00:29:09.470 --> 00:29:11.070
It'll be fun.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:15.940
Hey.

00:29:15.940 --> 00:29:17.160
Hey.

00:29:17.970 --> 00:29:20.540
So, you find out where
the electrician's buried?

00:29:20.540 --> 00:29:21.940
He wasn't.

00:29:21.940 --> 00:29:23.600
Billy beard was cremated.

00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:25.500
Great.

00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:26.940
Now what?

00:29:26.940 --> 00:29:28.280
No idea.

00:29:28.400 --> 00:29:30.660
Anymore ghost cameos in the dailies?

00:29:30.660 --> 00:29:33.090
Not in the first six hours.

00:29:34.270 --> 00:29:34.960
You know.

00:29:34.960 --> 00:29:39.110
Maybe the spirits are trying to shut
down the movie 'cause they think it sucks.

00:29:39.110 --> 00:29:40.640
'Cause, I mean, it kind of does.

00:29:40.640 --> 00:29:43.300
From, uh, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:29:43.300 --> 00:29:44.090
Come on.

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:45.450
It'll be fun.

00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:03.600
Listen to the invocation.

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:08.310
Dean, that's the real deal a
necromantic summoning ritual.

00:30:11.430 --> 00:30:14.100
What the hell is that
doing in a hollywood movie?

00:30:14.100 --> 00:30:14.550
No, dear.

00:30:14.550 --> 00:30:15.830
We're down for a few days.

00:30:15.830 --> 00:30:20.490
It's cool, it gives me time to
pitch that time-Travel thing.

00:30:20.840 --> 00:30:21.690
Yeah.

00:30:21.730 --> 00:30:22.300
All right, well, look.

00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:23.320
Get back to me on this, all right?

00:30:23.320 --> 00:30:24.180
Seriously.

00:30:24.180 --> 00:30:25.920
No, I'm serious.

00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:27.020
Dude, are you serious?

00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:28.420
'Cause I'm serious.

00:30:28.420 --> 00:30:29.590
All right.

00:30:29.590 --> 00:30:30.710
Cool.

00:30:31.010 --> 00:30:31.930
Guys, we're all shut down.

00:30:31.930 --> 00:30:33.070
What are you still doing here?

00:30:33.070 --> 00:30:34.660
Yeah, uh...

00:30:34.660 --> 00:30:36.580
Really sorry, man.

00:30:36.580 --> 00:30:39.040
We -- We -- We
couldn't help ourselves.

00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:41.840
We just had to tell you
that we read the script.

00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:42.910
And?

00:30:43.830 --> 00:30:45.100
Yeah.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:47.400
It's, uh...

00:30:47.400 --> 00:30:48.300
It's awesome.

00:30:48.300 --> 00:30:49.500
Awesome.

00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:50.640
Really awesome.

00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:51.050
I know.

00:30:51.050 --> 00:30:52.200
It's pretty rockin', right?

00:30:52.200 --> 00:30:53.340
I'm glad you guys liked it.

00:30:53.340 --> 00:30:53.940
Yeah.

00:30:53.940 --> 00:30:56.740
I-I really liked all
the attention to detail.

00:30:56.740 --> 00:30:57.250
Dude, right on.

00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:57.770
That's my thing.

00:30:57.770 --> 00:31:00.060
I mean, you know, color
me guilty, but that is me.

00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:01.830
I'm a total detail buff.

00:31:01.830 --> 00:31:07.670
No, I mean, the way you worked in all those Enochian
summoning rituals and all the authentic language and...

00:31:07.670 --> 00:31:09.750
What, you mean that latin crap?

00:31:11.930 --> 00:31:12.480
No, man.

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:13.670
That's Walter.

00:31:13.670 --> 00:31:15.790
Walter Dixon, the original writer.

00:31:15.790 --> 00:31:17.320
You like that garbage?

00:31:17.320 --> 00:31:18.880
Wait, Walter --
The P.A.Walter?

00:31:18.880 --> 00:31:19.920
No, he's not a P.A.

00:31:19.940 --> 00:31:22.860
He's got a clause in his contract
that allows him to come on set.

00:31:22.860 --> 00:31:24.410
But he wrote the invocations?

00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:26.120
He wrote a wackjob screenplay.

00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:26.790
There's no pace.

00:31:26.790 --> 00:31:27.890
There's no love interest.

00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:29.390
It's all wackadoo exposition.

00:31:29.390 --> 00:31:33.570
I had to cut, like, 90% of it to make
it readable, another 10% to make it good.

00:31:37.970 --> 00:31:39.850
Should have kept
Walter's original script.

00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:41.110
It's actually pretty good.

00:31:41.110 --> 00:31:42.720
Yeah.

00:31:44.100 --> 00:31:46.770
And it reads like a how-To
manual of conjuration,

00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:50.720
Like a textbook on how to summon ghosts
and get them to do whatever you want.

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:51.940
Yeah, like kill people.

00:31:51.950 --> 00:31:53.270
Yep.

00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:57.510
So let's say somewhere down the line,
Walter learned some pretty black magic.

00:31:57.510 --> 00:32:01.120
Yeah, and let's say he's pissed at
these people for wrecking his movie.

00:32:01.380 --> 00:32:02.500
Motive and means.

00:32:03.010 --> 00:32:04.680
It's worth checking out.

00:32:14.620 --> 00:32:15.490
So?

00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:18.190
You wanted to meet?

00:32:20.870 --> 00:32:22.300
Hey, I'm a little busy here, buddy.

00:32:22.520 --> 00:32:23.570
I'm working on a script.

00:32:23.810 --> 00:32:24.070
Oh, yeah.

00:32:24.070 --> 00:32:25.820
You guys worked on it a lot.

00:32:25.820 --> 00:32:27.360
It needed work.

00:32:27.360 --> 00:32:29.130
Now, why couldn't we have
done this in my office?

00:32:29.130 --> 00:32:34.080
You know, the history, the lore in
my draft was completely accurate.

00:32:34.080 --> 00:32:40.900
We could have gotten it right for the first time ever
in this whorehouse of a town, but you tore it to shreds.

00:32:41.650 --> 00:32:45.020
You replaced it with
cleavage and fart jokes.

00:32:46.440 --> 00:32:47.680
It was real.

00:32:47.680 --> 00:32:50.110
Who gives a rat's ass about real?

00:32:50.110 --> 00:32:51.420
We're talking about ghosts here, Walter.

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:52.350
There's no such thing.

00:32:52.350 --> 00:32:54.380
That's where you're wrong, martin.

00:33:06.310 --> 00:33:07.560
Okay, nutjob...

00:33:07.560 --> 00:33:08.860
End of meeting.

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:19.950
C oh, my god, no!

00:33:19.950 --> 00:33:21.500
Please, no!

00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:23.250
You ruined it, martin!

00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:24.850
Everything I worked for!

00:33:24.850 --> 00:33:27.040
Oh, god!

00:33:27.370 --> 00:33:28.080
Walter!

00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:30.660
Now you're gonna find out
what being a ghost is like!

00:33:30.660 --> 00:33:32.160
Walter, please!

00:33:32.160 --> 00:33:34.180
Walter, help me!

00:33:34.630 --> 00:33:36.030
Help!

00:33:44.950 --> 00:33:46.890
You are one hell of a P.A.

00:33:46.890 --> 00:33:48.440
Yeah, I know.

00:33:50.770 --> 00:33:52.060
What are you doing?

00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:53.930
Could ask you the same thing, Walter.

00:33:53.930 --> 00:33:55.490
Raising these spirits from the dead?

00:33:56.830 --> 00:33:57.800
Making them murder for you?

00:33:57.800 --> 00:33:59.730
That's playing with fire, Walter.

00:33:59.730 --> 00:34:01.530
You don't understand.

00:34:02.700 --> 00:34:03.070
You know what?

00:34:03.070 --> 00:34:03.550
You're right.

00:34:03.550 --> 00:34:04.950
I don't understand.

00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:08.100
Wait, look.

00:34:08.100 --> 00:34:12.710
You put your heart and soul into
something, years of hard work ... years.

00:34:12.710 --> 00:34:16.330
And then they take it,
and they crap all over it!

00:34:17.330 --> 00:34:20.550
And then -- And then they want
you to smile and say thank you.

00:34:20.550 --> 00:34:21.170
Walter, listen.

00:34:21.170 --> 00:34:22.000
It's just a movie.

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:23.170
That's it.

00:34:26.790 --> 00:34:27.660
Look.

00:34:29.690 --> 00:34:31.070
I got nothing against you, man.

00:34:31.070 --> 00:34:32.000
You're not part of this.

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:34.290
Just please --
Please, just leave.

00:34:34.970 --> 00:34:36.320
But martin's got to stay.

00:34:36.520 --> 00:34:37.900
Sorry, can't do that.

00:34:38.230 --> 00:34:39.500
It's not that we like him or anything.

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:41.830
It's a matter of principle.

00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:43.520
Then I'm sorry, too.

00:34:44.690 --> 00:34:45.520
Walter.

00:34:45.520 --> 00:34:47.670
Walter,
pl-- Don't.

00:35:08.010 --> 00:35:09.410
Sam!

00:35:19.200 --> 00:35:19.750
Come on.

00:35:19.750 --> 00:35:21.060
Come on.

00:35:31.190 --> 00:35:33.080
Come out to the coast.

00:35:46.960 --> 00:35:50.500
We'll get together, have a few laughs.

00:35:55.880 --> 00:35:57.000
Oh, man!

00:35:58.590 --> 00:35:59.520
I can't frickin' believe this.

00:35:59.520 --> 00:36:00.530
Ghosts are real.

00:36:00.530 --> 00:36:01.870
What makes you say that?

00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:13.320
But I don't understand.

00:36:13.510 --> 00:36:15.510
How is Walter controlling them?

00:36:15.650 --> 00:36:17.310
Probably that talisman.

00:36:24.580 --> 00:36:25.430
What are you doing?

00:36:25.430 --> 00:36:28.180
If film cameras pick
these suckers up, then...

00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:29.980
Maybe, uh...

00:36:35.400 --> 00:36:36.710
Dean, right there!

00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:43.650
Hey!

00:36:43.650 --> 00:36:44.920
Right there!

00:36:50.360 --> 00:36:50.770
Here.

00:36:50.770 --> 00:36:51.400
Get the idea?

00:36:51.400 --> 00:36:51.870
Yeah.

00:36:51.870 --> 00:36:52.720
All right, you hold them off.

00:36:52.720 --> 00:36:54.210
I'm going after Walter.

00:36:59.190 --> 00:37:00.980
I cannot believe there's an afterlife.

00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:02.720
There's an afterlife, all right.

00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:04.750
But mostly it's a pain in the ass.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:07.470
There!

00:37:11.830 --> 00:37:14.790
It's over, Walter.

00:37:18.490 --> 00:37:19.480
TherE.

00:37:19.620 --> 00:37:21.310
Okay, now no one can have it.

00:37:23.840 --> 00:37:25.610
I wouldn't have done that if I were you.

00:37:25.610 --> 00:37:26.860
Yeah?

00:37:26.860 --> 00:37:27.930
Why not?

00:37:28.030 --> 00:37:29.510
'Cause you just freed them.

00:37:30.370 --> 00:37:32.100
We can't stop them now.

00:37:32.540 --> 00:37:34.260
Walter, you brought them back...

00:37:34.990 --> 00:37:36.420
Forced them to murder.

00:37:36.800 --> 00:37:38.760
They're not going to
be very happy with you.

00:37:38.760 --> 00:37:40.090
Yeah?

00:37:40.410 --> 00:37:41.480
So, why not?

00:38:03.170 --> 00:38:06.510
Oh, god.

00:38:08.530 --> 00:38:09.620
There!

00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:12.290
But I don't understand.

00:38:12.570 --> 00:38:14.630
How come the spirits
appear in the camera phone?

00:38:14.630 --> 00:38:17.600
The video must pick up their
frequencies in a way that our eyes can't.

00:38:20.330 --> 00:38:21.730
Oh, God.

00:38:21.850 --> 00:38:22.900
Right there!

00:38:25.460 --> 00:38:26.190
Cut!

00:38:26.190 --> 00:38:27.760
Oh, print that one.

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:28.990
That's in the movie.

00:38:28.990 --> 00:38:29.630
Oh!

00:38:29.630 --> 00:38:31.220
Loved it, kids,  loved it!

00:38:35.010 --> 00:38:37.920
You find out there's an afterlife,
and this is what you do with it?

00:38:38.980 --> 00:38:40.870
<i>I needed a little jazz on the page.</i>

00:39:00.740 --> 00:39:02.410
You're one hell of a P.A.

00:39:04.080 --> 00:39:05.130
Thank you.

00:39:08.190 --> 00:39:09.180
Hi.

00:39:33.520 --> 00:39:34.890
<i>God, I love this town.</i>



